# HTTP requests (D49, D101, D116B) and WebSockets (D106) on the web: option
# blocks, started requests and their handlers, websocket handlers and
# states, at the top level and inside a function.
base is "https://example.com"
get base into page
    with header "X-One" is "1"
    with header "X-Two" is "2"
    with cookies
    following redirects
get json from base into data
    with timeout 5 seconds
get base as json into other
post "hello" to base into answer
    without cookies
    without redirects
post data as json to base
put "x" to base into putAnswer
    with timeout 2 seconds
put data as json to base
delete from base into gone1
delete from base into gone2
    with header "Authorization" is "token"
start get from base and call it first
start post "x" as json to base and call it second
    with header "X" is "y"
on complete of first
    say "done:" received response
.
on error of first
    say "failed"
.
on cancel of second
    say "cancelled"
.
if first is pending or second is completed
    say "states"
.
if first is failed or first is cancelled
    say "more states"
.
cancel second
connect to websocket "wss://example.com/chat" using protocol "chat" and call it socket
connect to websocket "wss://example.com/plain" and call it plain
on open of socket
    send "hi" through socket
.
on message from socket
    say received message
.
on close of socket
    say close code close reason close was clean
.
on error of socket
    say websocket error
.
if socket is open or socket is connecting or plain is closed or plain is closing
    say "socket states"
.
close websocket socket
close websocket plain with code 1001 and reason "bye"
to fetchIt url
    get url into body
    post body to url into reply
    start get from url and call it later
    connect to websocket "wss://example.com/x" and call it inner
    on message from inner
        say received message
    .
    return reply
say fetchIt base
